Enterprise Specification & Technical Problem Statement1. Business Context & Operational DomainFinSecure Global operates as a Tier-1 financial transaction processing network handling high-frequency interbank settlements, foreign currency exchanges, corporate securities disbursements, and automated fraud-compliance monitoring. The network interfaces with real-time gross settlement (RTGS) streams, the Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial Telecommunication (SWIFT), and Automated Clearing House (ACH) rails.The network operations center requires a resilient, deterministic, memory-efficient core processing hub: the FinSecure Engine. The engine must ingest structured and unstructured telemetry streams, validate transaction integrity against strict protocol specifications, compute dynamic risk scores, evaluate foreign exchange tariffs, buffer incoming transactions in a fixed-capacity staging pipeline, audit records concurrently, format regional currencies, and settle funds into customer balances without memory leaks or race conditions.To meet financial regulatory standards, the engine must be implemented in Java, conforming strictly to language specifications across memory architecture, type safety, flow control, object-oriented design, error recovery, pattern matching, and multi-threaded string manipulation.2. Functional & Business Domain Requirements                       INCOMING TELEMETRY STREAM
