2.1 Ingestion & Payload ValidationProtocol Ingestion: The engine must read raw telemetry streams over socket connections formatted as:$$\text{TXN-}\langle\text{AlphanumericCode}\rangle\text{;VAL=}\langle\text{DecimalAmount}\rangle\text{;CUR=}\langle\text{3-Letter ISO Currency}\rangle$$Pattern Matching: Payload segments must be parsed using precompiled regular expressions with named-capturing groups (txCode, val, cur).Validation Guards: If an incoming message fails regex structure, contains an invalid currency denomination, or specifies a negative/zero amount, the system must abort processing and raise a checked InvalidPayloadException.2.2 Staging Queue & Capacity InvariantsConveyor Buffer: Due to hardware memory limits on line-rate settlement cards, incoming transactions must be held in a fixed-capacity staging array with a strict limit of $N = 3$ slots.Overflow Handling: When a transaction arrives and all staging slots are occupied, the engine must reject the packet immediately by throwing an unchecked LedgerCapacityExceededException without blocking the main event loop.Buffer De-staging: As transactions are cleared, the corresponding array slots must be reset to null to permit timely garbage reclamation of completed payload references.2.3 Tariff Computation, Risk Scoring, & Anti-Money Laundering (AML)Transaction Classification: Transactions are grouped into three distinct categories, each with its own tariff schedule:DOMESTIC_TRANSFER: Base fee of $5.00, standard tariff multiplier of $1.0\times$.CROSS_BORDER: Base fee of $25.00, risk multiplier of $2.5\times$.SECURITIES_SETTLEMENT: Base fee of $100.00, risk multiplier of $4.0\times$.Compliance Thresholds: Transactions with an aggregate settlement sum exceeding $100,000.00 must incur an additional $50.00 high-volume audit fee; otherwise, a baseline $10.00 documentation fee is assessed.AML Anomaly Tripping: Any transaction that is both classified as CROSS_BORDER and carries a gross value exceeding $250,000.00 must trigger an automated AML anomaly flag (isSuspicious = true) for compliance auditing.2.4 Multilateral Settlement & Payment InstrumentsAccount Ledger Updates: Validated transactions must deposit settled funds directly into the recipient's BankAccount. Credit-based card transactions must run through an abstract payment hierarchy to verify credit limit headroom before approval.Dual-Track Audit Logging:Single-threaded transaction digests must be constructed via StringBuilder for maximum string-concatenation performance.Multi-threaded, shared operational ledgers must be logged via StringBuffer to guarantee thread safety.Localization: Final settlement receipts must produce currency formats localized for the United States (Locale.US), Germany (Locale.GERMANY), and India (new Locale("en", "IN")).

